  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 30 January 2008, the erection of a dormer window measuring 5.4m in width, 3m in height and 3.7m in depth and the hip-to-gable extension measuring 4m along the ridge, 3.3m in height and 8.1m across the flank and a roof light on the front plane of the roof of the house was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A and B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the extension is not over 50m3, and would not take developments on site over 70m3.\r\n"
